    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-q/q2",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q2-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The events A and B are such so that P ( A ∩ B′ ) = 0.25 ,     ( ) P A = 2P ( ) B and     ( P A ∪ B ) = 0.45 . Determine … a) … ( ) P A ∩ B . ( ) 5 b) … ( P A ∪ B′ ) . ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:592.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q2-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The union is the disjoint sum of A ∩B′ and B, so P(B) = 0.45 −0.25 . [B1] [A1] = 0.20 Then P(A) = 0.40 [A1] and P(A ∩B) = 0.40 −0.25 . [M1] [A1] = 0.15\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q2-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) Alternatively sum the regions belonging to A ∪B′: 0.25 + 0.15 + 0.55 = 0.95. The complement A′ ∩B has probability 0.20 −0.15 = 0.05, [B1] giving P(A ∪B′) = 0.95 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 2 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The events A and B are such so that P ( A ∩ B′ ) = 0.25 ,     ( ) P A = 2P ( ) B and     ( P A ∪ B ) = 0.45 . Determine … a) … ( ) P A ∩ B . ( ) 5 b) … ( P A ∪ B′ ) . ( ) 2"
