    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-q/q3",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q3-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The table below shows the marks obtained by a group of students, in two separate tests. Student A B C D E F G H Test 1 28 39 18 30 42 43 33 10 Test 2 12 23 16 16 28 18 24 7 The first test is out of 50 marks while the second test is out of 30 marks. Let x and y represent the marks obtained in Test 1 and Test 2 , respectively. a) Use a statistical calculator to find the value of the product moment correlation coefficient between x and y . ( ) 1\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q3-question-2.svg\" alt=\"b) Explain how the value of the product moment correlation coefficient between x and y will be affected if the individual test marks were converted into percentage marks. ( ) 1 c) Test, at the 1% level of significance, whether there is evidence of positive correlation between x and y . ( ) 3 A student was absent from the second test but he obtained 30 marks in the first test. d) Use linear regression to estimate this student’s mark in the second test. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The sample coefficient is r = 0.78890097 . . . . [A1] (b) Converting to percentages multiplies each variable by a positive constant. This keeps the correlation coefficient unchanged: [A1] (c) Setting hypothesis: Test H0 : ρ = 0 against H1 : ρ &gt; 0. [B1] The one-tailed 1% critical value for n = 8 is about 0.7887. [A1] Since r is slightly larger, reject H0. The sample provides evidence of positive correlation at 1% . [A1] (d) Regression of y on x gives ˆy ≈3.96171 + 0.462166x. [B1] Substitution gives 3.96171 + 0.462166(30) = 3.96171 + 13.86498\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"= 17.82669 At x = 30 this gives 17.83, or about 18 [A1] marks: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:501.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
