    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"2 The random variable Y is Normally distributed with mean µ and variance σ . Given that ( P Y &lt; 48 ) = P ( Y &gt; 57 ) = 0.0668 , find the value of  ( P 50.1 &lt; Y &lt; 55.8 ) . ( ) 9\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Equal tails give µ = (48 + 57)/2 . [B1] [M1] [A1] = 52.5 Since Φ(1.5) ≈0.9332, the standard deviation is approximately (57 −52.5)/1.5 = 3. [M1] [M1] [A1] The standard scores for the requested endpoints are (50.1 −52.5)/3 = −0.8 and (55.8 −52.5)/3 = 1.1.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-q/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Equivalently subtract the two outside tails from 1. Then P(50.1 &lt; Y &lt; 55.8) ≈Φ(1.1) −Φ(−0.8) ≈0.6525 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 9 marks.</p>"
